# ---- 7b. Read the four dashboards -------------------------------------------

### RF-1 — monthly expenses for 2026-07
### Expect rows: "P7 Groceries" 5000, "P7 Rent" 30000, "P7 Snacks" 2000, "P7 Shared Dining" 9000
### (both shared expenses debit their holder share to the same bucket: 5000 + 4000), and — RF-1 LEAK —
### "P7 Card Purchases" 12000 riding along in the "debit & cash" summary. Every row month "2026-07", currencyCode "ARS".
GET {{reports}}/monthly-expenses?month=2026-07
Accept: application/json

### Same query, unfiltered — every month, newest first
GET {{reports}}/monthly-expenses
Accept: application/json

### RF-2 — card due by month
### Accrued bucket: { "bucket": "Accrued", "card": "P7 Manual Card Liability", "cycleYear": null, "amountMinorUnits": 12000 }
###   (plus "P7 Visa Liability" 0 — auto-provisioned with the card, nothing accrued on it yet)
### Future bucket: 3 rows { "bucket": "Future", "card": "<p7Card GUID>", "cycleYear": 2026/2027, "cycleMonth": 12/1/2 } summing to 300000
### RF-2 GAP: Accrued.card is the Ledger account NAME; Future.card is the Financing CardId GUID, and it comes back
### UPPERCASE (raw EF/SQLite text) while any id a client got from a POST response is lowercase — no shared, case-safe key.
GET {{reports}}/card-due-by-month
Accept: application/json

### RF-7 — Alice's current-account timeline; expect exactly 2 rows, oldest first:
###   { "description": "Shared expense", "deltaMinorUnits": 5000,  "runningBalanceMinorUnits": 5000 }
###   { "description": "Settlement",     "deltaMinorUnits": -5000, "runningBalanceMinorUnits": 0 }
GET {{reports}}/parties/{{p7Alice.response.body.$.id}}/timeline
Accept: application/json

### Debt summary — one row per party with movements (GROUP BY collapses Alice's 2 movements into 1)
### Expect: { "partyName": "P7 Alice", "netBalanceMinorUnits": 0 } and { "partyName": "P7 Bob", "netBalanceMinorUnits": 4000 }
GET {{reports}}/parties/debt-summary
Accept: application/json

